&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is part of the Sony Group and responsible for the marketing, sales, and distribution of PlayStation hardware, software, services, and digital content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and strategic Sr. IT SOX Governance Lead to establish and drive end-to-end ownership of IT SOX governance within DTIS Global Service Operations (GSO). This role will serve as the primary lead responsible for IT General Controls (ITGC) governance, control framework ownership, audit coordination, onboarding of new systems, and governance standardization across the enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is critical to scaling IT governance capabilities, reducing operational risk, and enabling sustainable compliance operations as SIE continues to grow. The ideal candidate will combine deep SOX and ITGC expertise with strong governance leadership, operational execution, and cross-functional collaboration skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IT SOX Governance Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the IT SOX governance framework and ITGC program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standardized governance processes, methodologies, and control design practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end ownership of ITGC lifecycle activities including design, implementation, onboarding, testing support, remediation tracking, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive governance consistency across systems, applications, and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control Design &amp;amp; Framework Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, document, and maintain ITGCs and application controls aligned to SOX requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable governance standards for onboarding new systems and processes into SOX scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain control narratives, process documentation, data flows, and supporting evidence standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with control owners to improve effectiveness and operational maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit &amp;amp; Compliance Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary IT interface for external and internal audit stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate walkthroughs, evidence collection, testing support, and remediation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage audit findings, deficiencies, and corrective action plans through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely and accurate delivery of audit artifacts and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Assessment &amp;amp; Operational Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct risk assessments and identify control gaps, process inefficiencies, and governance risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop remediation and mitigation strategies for identified deficiencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor compliance status, control performance, and governance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement initiatives focused on automation, scalability, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering, infrastructure, platform operations, Finance Governance (FinGov), and Risk &amp;amp; Compliance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support alignment between SOX governance and other compliance programs including PCI, GDPR, and security governance initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive governance accountability and awareness across technical and operational stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance Transformation &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for automation and process optimization within SOX operations and evidence management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to long-term governance roadmap initiatives including continuous monitoring capabilities and scalable onboarding models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on regulatory requirements, industry trends, and governance best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Information Technology, Accounting, Computer Science, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in IT SOX, IT audit, IT governance, compliance, or risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in SOX compliance, IT General Controls (ITGCs), and audit coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading governance programs and working directly with external/internal auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with control design, system scope assessments, system onboarding, and remediation management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system implementation framework (SDLC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big 4 experience supporting SOX audits and IT General Controls (ITGC) assessments preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as CISA, CISSP, CISM, CRISC, or CPA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Optro SoxHub or similar governance/audit platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with cloud services and environments, along with knowledge of microservices architecture and CI/CD development techniques is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience auditing SAP ERP systems is preferred. Experience with S/4, GRC, BW and HANA databases in cloud deployments is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in ITGC reviews of complex architectures, across the many IT layers (Networking/OS/DB/App/Tools), and with broad practice in various technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting large-scale enterprise environments and operational governance transformation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with process automation and governance tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PlayStation, we value diversity and believe that a diverse workforce leads to a more successful and innovative company. We are an equal opportunity employer (EOE) and welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you require any reasonable accommodations or adjustments throughout the application process, please let us know and we will be happy to assist you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us at PlayStation and be part of a team that is dedicated to delivering exceptional gaming experiences to millions of players worldwide. Apply now and embark on a journey of professional growth and fulfillment!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$127,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,600 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
